> Often, force bolt is an important part of the XL1-2 wizard's survival--
> kill those werejackals quickly before they summon help.

For a while I practiced force bolt on doors and everything else
in my way to practice attack spells to be able to #enhance
that school ASAP.  The result was hunger problems and
active nymphs.  Force bolted doors wake up nymphs it
seems.  Since I figured that out I still use force bolt as a
weapon especially on monsters mean for my current level,
but I don't use it to the point I often run out of energy.

> Once you can
> find some mithril it's probably worth wearing, but your spells aren't
> completely useless.

I wear mithril until studded leather appears.  A strong
enough pet will attack the regular watchmen in mine
town and they often wear studded leather.  So let your
pet attack lots of monsters so it is strong enough.  I
am not sure it's a good idea to switch to mithril as soon
as mine town going down or if it's better to switch to it
in mine town coming back up.

Dagger skill is so important I'll name Sting early on and
use it for fleeing melee.



